Changes to GCC 15.2.0 for libstdc++ compiled by clang, for the Windows
sysroots of clang-retro/win32-sdk (scripts/build-libstdcxx.sh).

- eh_globals.cc: clang wants an initializer for constant initialization.
- eh_personality.cc: <windows.h> for the SEH personality (x86_64), which
  clang's <unwind.h> does not include.
- tinfo.cc: clang does not accept the alias attribute on the declaration
  of a member function; type_info::__equal is a definition.
- assert_fail.cc: the same noreturn attribute as the first declaration.
- random.cc: clang's name for the 32-bit rdseed built-in.
- string-inst.cc: the copy-on-write string's data() is not noexcept.
- experimental/bits/fs_path.h: clang checks the non-dependent throw of
  filesystem_error in a template before the class is complete.
- src/c++11/Makefile: no -gno-as-loc-support, which is GCC's only.
- os_defines.h (mingw-w64): below XP (_WIN32_WINNT 0x0501), no
  GetModuleHandleExW for thread_local destructors and no rand_s, which
  calls LoadLibraryW and RtlGenRandom.
- chrono.cc: below 2000, system_clock looks up GetSystemTimeAsFileTime at
  run time, as NT 3.1 and Win32s do not have it.
- basic_file_stdio.cc: below 2000, a wide file name is opened with the
  _wfopen found at run time on NT, and converted to the ANSI code page on
  95, 98 and ME, where _wfopen is a stub.
- gthr-win32.h: condition variables below Vista with the functions of
  gthr-win32-compat.c (__GTHREAD_WIN32_COMPAT), which free them.
